# Review assignment (#233).
#
# One maintainer, so one line -- and it is here rather than nowhere because a
# CODEOWNERS file is what makes a review request arrive instead of a pull
# request sitting unread. The day there is a second maintainer, this is the file
# that splits by directory; until then a per-path table would be four ways of
# writing the same name.
#
# It assigns a reviewer. It does not require one: `require_code_owner_reviews`
# is off in docs/PUBLIC_BRANCH_PROTECTION.toml, because with a single account a
# review requirement is a lock whose key is in the same pocket.
